				<p>{t('ocx init writes a provider into your Codex config and shares one model catalog with Codex CLI, TUI, App, and SDK. On a standalone owner, ocx stop restores native Codex; linked clients and siblings retain their shared routing.', 'ocx init이 Codex 설정에 프로바이더를 추가하고, Codex CLI·TUI·App·SDK가 하나의 모델 카탈로그를 함께 씁니다. 독립 실행 소유 인스턴스에서는 ocx stop이 기본 Codex를 복원합니다. 연결된 클라이언트와 형제 인스턴스의 공유 라우팅은 유지됩니다.', 'ocx init 将 provider 写入 Codex 配置，CLI、TUI、App 与 SDK 共享同一模型目录。在独立所有者实例上，ocx stop 恢复原生 Codex；已连接客户端和兄弟实例保留共享路由。', 'ocx init записывает провайдера в конфигурацию Codex, а Codex CLI, TUI, App и SDK используют общий каталог моделей. В автономном экземпляре-владельце ocx stop восстанавливает нативный Codex; связанные клиенты и соседние экземпляры сохраняют общую маршрутизацию.', 'ocx init が Codex 設定にプロバイダーを書き込み、Codex CLI・TUI・App・SDK で 1 つのモデルカタログを共有します。独立した所有インスタンスでは ocx stop がネイティブ Codex を復元します。リンク済みクライアントと兄弟インスタンスの共有ルーティングは維持されます。', 'ocx init 將供應商寫入 Codex 設定，CLI、TUI、App 與 SDK 共享同一模型目錄。在獨立擁有者執行個體上，ocx stop 會還原原生 Codex；已連結用戶端和同層執行個體保留共用路由。', 'ocx init, Codex yapılandırmanıza bir sağlayıcı yazar; Codex CLI, TUI, App ve SDK aynı model kataloğunu paylaşır. Bağımsız sahip örnekte ocx stop yerel Codex’i geri yükler; bağlı istemciler ve kardeş örnekler ortak yönlendirmeyi korur.')}</p>
				<div class="lp-terminal">
					<div class="lp-terminal-bar"><span>zsh</span></div>
					<pre>{quickstart.map((line) => (<code><span class="lp-prompt">$ </span>{line.cmd}<span class="lp-note">  # {line.note}</span>{'\n'}</code>))}</pre>
				</div>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<div class="lp-github-row">
		<div class="lp-cloud-cta">
			<Image src={heroFieldLight} alt="" class="lp-field-light" loading="lazy" widths={[1024, 2048]} sizes="100vw" />
			<Image src={heroFieldDark} alt="" class="lp-field-dark" loading="lazy" widths={[1024, 2048]} sizes="100vw" />
			<CloudCanvas variant="overlay" />
		</div>
		<a class="lp-github-cta" href={GITHUB_URL} aria-label={githubAccessibleName}
			data-gh-stars-label={starLabel} data-gh-stars-locale={starLocale}>
			<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d={siGithub.path} /></svg>
			<span>{githubCta}</span>
			{starCount !== null && <span data-gh-stars={starCount}>{formatStarCount(starCount)}</span>}
		</a>
	</div>

	<!-- full docs sitemap band: every section reachable from the landing -->
	<section class="lp-next" id="docs-map" aria-label={t('Documentation map', '문서 맵', '文档地图', 'Карта документации', 'ドキュメントマップ', '文件地圖', 'Dokümantasyon haritası')}>
		<h2>{t('Explore the docs', '문서 살펴보기', '浏览文档', 'Изучите документацию', 'ドキュメントを探る', '瀏覽文件', 'Dokümantasyonu Keşfedin')}</h2>
		<div class="lp-next-grid">
			{docsMap.map((group) => (
				<div class="lp-next-col">
					<h3><svg class="lp-ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d={icons[group.icon]} /></svg>{group.label}</h3>
					<ul>
						{group.links.map((link) => (
							<li><a href={link.href}>{link.label}</a></li>
						))}
					</ul>
				</div>
			))}
		</div>
	</section>

	<p class="lp-disclaimer">
		{t(
			'opencodex is an independent community project, not affiliated with or endorsed by OpenAI, Anthropic, or any other provider. Some providers may restrict accounts that route traffic through third-party proxies — review each provider\u2019s Terms of Service before connecting.',
			'opencodex는 독립 커뮤니티 프로젝트로, OpenAI, Anthropic 등 어떤 프로바이더와도 제휴 관계가 없고 보증을 받지 않습니다. 일부 프로바이더는 서드파티 프록시를 거친 트래픽이 있는 계정을 제한할 수 있으니, 연결하기 전에 각 프로바이더의 이용약관을 확인하세요.',
			'opencodex 是独立的社区项目，与 OpenAI、Anthropic 或任何其他提供商均无关联或背书。部分提供商可能限制经第三方代理路由流量的账号 —— 连接前请查阅各提供商的服务条款。',
			'opencodex — независимый проект сообщества, никак не связанный с OpenAI, Anthropic или любым другим провайдером и не одобренный ими. Некоторые провайдеры могут ограничивать аккаунты, направляющие трафик через сторонние прокси, — перед подключением ознакомьтесь с условиями обслуживания каждого провайдера.',
			'opencodex は独立したコミュニティプロジェクトであり、OpenAI、Anthropic などいかなるプロバイダーとも提携・推奨されるものではありません。一部のプロバイダーはサードパーティプロキシ経由のトラフィックを使用するアカウントを制限する可能性があります — 接続前に各プロバイダーの利用規約を確認してください。',
			'opencodex 是獨立的社群專案，與 OpenAI、Anthropic 或任何其他供應商均無關聯或背書。部分供應商可能限制經第三方代理路由流量的帳號 —— 連線前請查閱各供應商的服務條款。',
			'opencodex bağımsız bir topluluk projesidir; OpenAI, Anthropic veya başka bir sağlayıcı ile bağlantılı veya onlar tarafından onaylanmış değildir. Bazı sağlayıcılar trafiği üçüncü taraf proxy’ler üzerinden yönlendiren hesapları sınırlandırabilir — bağlanmadan önce her sağlayıcının Hizmet Şartlarını inceleyin.'
		)}
	</p>
</div>

<script>
	// Landing motion layer. Everything here is decoration on top of content
	// that is already fully visible: nothing is hidden until `cl-motion` lands
	// on <html>, and reduced motion never gets the class.
	//  - reveal: fade + 16px rise on the soft ease, staggered, once in view
	//  - split headings: section titles rise word by word out of a blur
	//  - hero depth: photo and clouds drift apart with pointer and scroll
	//  - cards: cursor spotlight + spring-smoothed tilt
	//  - magnetic CTAs and a counting star total
	const root = document.documentElement;
	const motionPreference = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
	const reduceMotion = motionPreference.matches;
	const finePointer = matchMedia('(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)').matches;
	const lerp = (a: number, b: number, k: number) => a + (b - a) * k;

	if (!reduceMotion) {
		root.classList.add('cl-motion');

		const revealGroups: [string, number][] = [
			['.lp-download-sub, .lp-download-version, .lp-dl-more, .lp-dl-foot', 0.08],
			['.lp-dl-grid > .lp-dl-card', 0.08],
			['.lp-scrub-stage, .lp-scrub-caption', 0.1],
			['.lp-grid > .lp-cell', 0.07],
			['.lp-github-row', 0],
			['.lp-next-grid > .lp-next-col', 0.07],
			['.lp-disclaimer', 0],
		];
		for (const [selector, step] of revealGroups) {
			document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(selector).forEach((el, i) => {
				el.dataset.reveal = '';
				el.style.setProperty('--rd', `${(i * step).toFixed(2)}s`);
			});
		}

		document
			.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.lp-download-title, .lp-bento-title, .lp-scrub-title, .lp-next h2')
			.forEach((heading) => {
				const text = heading.textContent ?? '';
				heading.setAttribute('aria-label', text);
				heading.textContent = '';
				text.split(/(\s+)/).forEach((part, i) => {
					if (/^\s+$/.test(part)) {
						heading.append(part);
						return;
					}
					const word = document.createElement('span');
					word.className = 'cl-word';
					word.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
					word.style.setProperty('--wd', `${(i / 2) * 0.045}s`);
					word.textContent = part;
					heading.append(word);
				});
				heading.dataset.reveal = '';
			});

		const io = new IntersectionObserver(
			(entries) => {
				for (const entry of entries) {
					if (!entry.isIntersecting) continue;
					entry.target.classList.add('is-in');
					io.unobserve(entry.target);
				}
			},
			{ rootMargin: '0px 0px -80px 0px' },
		);
		document.querySelectorAll('[data-reveal]').forEach((el) => io.observe(el));
	}

	// One shared animation loop; it sleeps whenever nothing is still settling.
	type Tick = () => boolean;
	const ticks = new Set<Tick>();
	let loopId = 0;
	const resetMotion: (() => void)[] = [];
	const frame = () => {
		loopId = 0;
		for (const tick of ticks) if (!tick()) ticks.delete(tick);
		if (ticks.size) loopId = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
	};
	const wake = (tick: Tick) => {
		if (motionPreference.matches) return;
		ticks.add(tick);
		loopId ||= requestAnimationFrame(frame);
	};
	motionPreference.addEventListener('change', () => {
		if (!motionPreference.matches) return;
		cancelAnimationFrame(loopId);
		loopId = 0;
		ticks.clear();
		root.classList.remove('cl-motion');
		resetMotion.forEach((reset) => reset());
	});

	// Hero depth: pointer parallax (fine pointers) + scroll drift.
	const hero = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.lp-hero-field');
	if (hero) {
		const target = { x: 0, y: 0, s: 0 };
		const cur = { x: 0, y: 0, s: 0 };
		resetMotion.push(() => {
			Object.assign(target, { x: 0, y: 0, s: 0 });
			Object.assign(cur, { x: 0, y: 0, s: 0 });
			['--px', '--py', '--sy'].forEach((name) => hero.style.removeProperty(name));
		});
		const tick: Tick = () => {
			cur.x = lerp(cur.x, target.x, 0.06);
			cur.y = lerp(cur.y, target.y, 0.06);
			cur.s = lerp(cur.s, target.s, 0.12);
			hero.style.setProperty('--px', cur.x.toFixed(4));
			hero.style.setProperty('--py', cur.y.toFixed(4));
			hero.style.setProperty('--sy', cur.s.toFixed(4));
			return Math.abs(cur.x - target.x) + Math.abs(cur.y - target.y) + Math.abs(cur.s - target.s) > 0.0005;
		};
		if (finePointer) {
			hero.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => {
				if (motionPreference.matches) return;
				const r = hero.getBoundingClientRect();
				target.x = ((e.clientX - r.left) / r.width) * 2 - 1;
				target.y = ((e.clientY - r.top) / r.height) * 2 - 1;
				wake(tick);
			});
			hero.addEventListener('pointerleave', () => {
				target.x = 0;
				target.y = 0;
				wake(tick);
			});
		}
		const onScroll = () => {
			if (motionPreference.matches) return;
			const r = hero.getBoundingClientRect();
			target.s = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, -r.top / Math.max(1, r.height)));
			wake(tick);
		};
		addEventListener('scroll', onScroll, { passive: true });
		onScroll();
	}

	// Cards: the hover glow drifts along the bottom edge under the cursor
	// (CSS eases `left`, so raw pointer positions are enough).
	if (finePointer) {
		document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.lp-cell').forEach((card) => {
			resetMotion.push(() => card.style.removeProperty('--mx'));
			card.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => {
				if (motionPreference.matches) return;
				const r = card.getBoundingClientRect();
				card.style.setProperty('--mx', `${(((e.clientX - r.left) / r.width) * 100).toFixed(1)}%`);
			});
			card.addEventListener('pointerleave', () => card.style.removeProperty('--mx'));
		});

		// Magnetic CTAs drift a few pixels toward the cursor.
		document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.lp-btn-primary, .lp-btn-ghost, .lp-github-cta').forEach((btn) => {
			const target = { x: 0, y: 0 };
			const cur = { x: 0, y: 0 };
			resetMotion.push(() => {
				Object.assign(target, { x: 0, y: 0 });
				Object.assign(cur, { x: 0, y: 0 });
				btn.style.removeProperty('--mgx');
				btn.style.removeProperty('--mgy');
			});
			const tick: Tick = () => {
				cur.x = lerp(cur.x, target.x, 0.18);
				cur.y = lerp(cur.y, target.y, 0.18);
				btn.style.setProperty('--mgx', `${cur.x.toFixed(2)}px`);
				btn.style.setProperty('--mgy', `${cur.y.toFixed(2)}px`);
				return Math.abs(cur.x - target.x) + Math.abs(cur.y - target.y) > 0.05;
			};
			btn.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => {
				if (motionPreference.matches) return;
				const r = btn.getBoundingClientRect();
				target.x = (e.clientX - (r.left + r.width / 2)) * 0.18;
				target.y = (e.clientY - (r.top + r.height / 2)) * 0.3;
				wake(tick);
			});
			btn.addEventListener('pointerleave', () => {
				target.x = 0;
				target.y = 0;
				wake(tick);
			});
		});
	}

	// Hero word roll. The CSS drum sizes its slot to the widest word, so the
	// shorter word left a gap or crowded the particle after it (worst in
	// Korean: "Codex를"). Here the slot takes each word's measured width and
	// eases between them while the words roll through a blur.
	const drum = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.lp-drum');
	if (drum) {
		const faces = Array.from(drum.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.lp-drum-spin .lp-drum-face')).slice(0, 2);
		const roll = document.createElement('span');
		roll.className = 'lp-roll';
		roll.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
		const words = faces.map((face, i) => {
			const word = document.createElement('span');
			word.className = `lp-roll-word ${face.className.replace('lp-drum-face', '').trim()}`;
			word.textContent = face.textContent;
			if (i === 0) word.classList.add('is-on');
			roll.append(word);
			return word;
		});
		drum.querySelector('.lp-drum-spin')?.replaceWith(roll);
		drum.classList.add('lp-drum-js');
		let index = 0;
		const fit = () => {
			if (motionPreference.matches) return;
			roll.style.width = `${words[index].getBoundingClientRect().width}px`;
		};
		// fonts swap in late; measure again once they have
		fit();
		document.fonts?.ready.then(fit);
		addEventListener('resize', fit, { passive: true });
		const HOLD_MS = 2600;
		let timer: ReturnType<typeof setInterval> | undefined;
		let cleanupTimer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined;
		const advance = () => {
			if (document.hidden) return;
			const prev = words[index];
			index = (index + 1) % words.length;
			const next = words[index];
			prev.classList.remove('is-on');
			prev.classList.add('is-out');
			next.classList.remove('is-out');
			next.classList.add('is-on');
			fit();
			cleanupTimer = setTimeout(() => prev.classList.remove('is-out'), 700);
		};
		const syncMotion = () => {
			clearInterval(timer);
			clearTimeout(cleanupTimer);
			timer = undefined;
			words.forEach((word) => word.classList.remove('is-out'));
			if (!motionPreference.matches) {
				fit();
				timer = setInterval(advance, HOLD_MS);
			}
		};
		motionPreference.addEventListener('change', syncMotion);
		syncMotion();
	}

	// The star total counts up once the closing panel comes into view, using
	// the same compact format the build renders (src/data/github-stars.ts).
	const stars = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.lp-github-cta [data-gh-stars]');
	const total = Number(stars?.dataset.ghStars);
	if (stars && Number.isFinite(total) && total > 0 && !reduceMotion) {
		const trim = (n: number) => String(n).replace(/\.0$/, '');
		const format = (n: number) =>
			n < 1000 ? String(n)
			: n < 100_000 ? `${trim(Math.floor(n / 100) / 10)}k`
			: n < 1_000_000 ? `${Math.floor(n / 1000)}k`
			: `${trim(Math.floor(n / 100_000) / 10)}m`;
		const final = stars.textContent;
		let starFrame = 0;
		const starObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries, obs) => {
			if (!entries.some((e) => e.isIntersecting)) return;
			obs.disconnect();
			if (motionPreference.matches) return;
			const start = performance.now();
			const DURATION = 1600;
			const step = (now: number) => {
				const t = Math.min(1, (now - start) / DURATION);
				const eased = t === 1 ? 1 : 1 - Math.pow(2, -10 * t);
				stars.textContent = t === 1 ? final : format(Math.round(total * eased));
				if (t < 1) starFrame = requestAnimationFrame(step);
			};
			starFrame = requestAnimationFrame(step);
		}, { threshold: 0.6 });
		starObserver.observe(stars);
		resetMotion.push(() => {
			starObserver.disconnect();
			cancelAnimationFrame(starFrame);
			stars.textContent = final;
		});
	}
</script>

<script>
	// Frame-sequence scrub (motion.md): the demo capture plays through as the
	// scrub scene scrolls. The poster remains until a frame is ready, and when
	// motion, viewport or scroll-timeline support makes the scrub unavailable.
	const canvas = document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('.lp-scrub-canvas');
	const section = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.lp-scene-scrub');
	const poster = document.querySelector<HTMLImageElement>('.lp-scrub-poster');
	const motionViewport = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) and (min-width: 48rem)');
	if (canvas && section && poster) {
		const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
		const count = Number(canvas.dataset.count || '0');
		const base = canvas.dataset.base || '/';
		const url = (i: number) => `${base}demo-frames/${String(i + 1).padStart(3, '0')}.webp`;
		const frames: (HTMLImageElement | undefined)[] = new Array(count);
		let started = false;
		let current = -1;
		let raf = 0;
		let generation = 0;
		let enabled = motionViewport.matches && CSS.supports('animation-timeline: view()');
		const load = (i: number) =>
			new Promise<void>((resolve) => {
				if (frames[i]) return resolve();
				const img = new Image();
				img.onload = () => { frames[i] = img; resolve(); };
				img.onerror = () => resolve();
				img.src = url(i);
			});
		const nearestLoaded = (i: number) => {
			for (let d = 0; d < count; d++) {
				if (frames[i - d]?.complete) return i - d;
				if (frames[i + d]?.complete) return i + d;
			}
			return -1;
		};
		const draw = (i: number) => {
			if (!enabled) return;
			const j = nearestLoaded(Math.max(0, Math.min(count - 1, i)));
			if (j < 0 || j === current || !ctx) return;
			current = j;
			const img = frames[j]!;
			if (canvas.width !== img.naturalWidth) {
				canvas.width = img.naturalWidth;
				canvas.height = img.naturalHeight;
			}
			ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
			ctx.drawImage(img, 0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
			poster.style.display = 'none';
			canvas.style.display = 'block';
		};
		const update = () => {
			raf = 0;
			if (!enabled || !section.hasAttribute('data-scrub-active')) return;
			const rect = section.getBoundingClientRect();
			const travel = section.offsetHeight - innerHeight;
			if (travel <= 0) return;
			const progress = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, -rect.top / travel));
			draw(Math.round(progress * (count - 1)));
		};
		const start = async () => {
			if (started || !enabled) return;
			started = true;
			const run = generation;
			await load(0);
			if (run !== generation || !enabled || !frames[0] || !ctx) return;
			// checkpoints first, then fill in idle time
			const checkpoints = [count - 1, Math.floor(count / 2), Math.floor(count / 4), Math.floor((3 * count) / 4)];
			await Promise.all(checkpoints.map(load));
			if (run !== generation || !enabled || !checkpoints.some((i) => i > 0 && frames[i])) return;
			draw(0);
			section.setAttribute('data-scrub-active', '');
			update();
			const fill = (i: number) => {
				if (run !== generation || !enabled || i >= count) return;
				load(i).then(() => {
					const next = () => fill(i + 1);
					'requestIdleCallback' in window ? requestIdleCallback(next) : setTimeout(next, 16);
				});
			};
			fill(0);
		};
		const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries, obs) => {
			if (entries.some((e) => e.isIntersecting)) { obs.disconnect(); start(); }
		}, { rootMargin: '100% 0px' });
		const reconcile = () => {
			generation++;
			observer.disconnect();
			cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
			raf = 0;
			started = false;
			current = -1;
			section.removeAttribute('data-scrub-active');
			canvas.style.display = 'none';
			poster.style.display = '';
			if (enabled) observer.observe(section);
		};
		motionViewport.addEventListener('change', (event) => {
			enabled = event.matches && CSS.supports('animation-timeline: view()');
			reconcile();
		});
		addEventListener('scroll', () => { if (enabled) raf ||= requestAnimationFrame(update); }, { passive: true });
		addEventListener('resize', () => { if (enabled) raf ||= requestAnimationFrame(update); }, { passive: true });
		reconcile();
	}
</script>

<script>
	// Desktop download surface: platform detection upgrades the hero CTA label
	// and flags the matching card; the latest-release fetch then swaps each
	// placeholder href for the real asset URL. Every step is optional — a
	// missing element, a failed fetch or a rate limit leaves the
	// server-rendered defaults (releases/latest) untouched.
	const uaPlatform = (navigator as Navigator & { userAgentData?: { platform?: string } })
		.userAgentData?.platform || navigator.userAgent || '';
	// Phones, tablets and ChromeOS cannot run the desktop builds; iOS user agents
	// also say "like Mac OS X", so they are ruled out before the desktop tests.
	// iPadOS in desktop mode reports a Mac user agent; a touch screen gives it away.
	const handheld = /iphone|ipad|ipod|android|cros|mobile/i.test(`${uaPlatform} ${navigator.userAgent}`)
		|| (/mac/i.test(uaPlatform) && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 1);
	const platform = handheld
		? ''
		: /mac/i.test(uaPlatform)
		? 'macos'
		: /win/i.test(uaPlatform)
			? 'windows'
			: /linux|x11/i.test(uaPlatform)
				? 'linux'
				: '';
	const recommend = (platform: string) => {
		const heroLabel = document.getElementById('lp-hero-download-label');
		const heroBtn = document.getElementById('lp-hero-download');
		const label = heroBtn?.dataset[`label${platform[0].toUpperCase()}${platform.slice(1)}`];
		if (heroLabel && label) heroLabel.textContent = label;
		const card = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`.lp-dl-card[data-platform="${platform}"]`);
		if (!card) return;
		card.setAttribute('data-recommended', '');
		// Show only this platform's card; the others move into the disclosure.
		// Without detection (or JavaScript) all three stay in the grid.
		const more = document.querySelector<HTMLDetailsElement>('.lp-dl-more');
		const moreGrid = more?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.lp-dl-more-grid');
		if (!more || !moreGrid) return;
		document
			.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.lp-dl-grid .lp-dl-card:not([data-recommended])')
			.forEach((other) => moreGrid.append(other));
		more.hidden = false;
	};
	// Linux builds are x86_64 only, so an ARM Linux desktop gets no recommendation.
	// Chromium freezes the Linux user agent to "x86_64", so its architecture hint
	// wins when present; other browsers report the real machine in the user agent.
	const uaData = (navigator as Navigator & {
		userAgentData?: { getHighEntropyValues?: (hints: string[]) => Promise<{ architecture?: string }> };
	}).userAgentData;
	if (platform === 'linux') {
		if (uaData?.getHighEntropyValues) {
			uaData
				.getHighEntropyValues(['architecture'])
				.then((hints) => { if (hints.architecture === 'x86') recommend('linux'); })
				.catch(() => {});
		} else if (/x86_64|amd64|x64/i.test(navigator.userAgent)) {
			recommend('linux');
		}
	} else if (platform) {
		recommend(platform);
	}
	fetch('https://api.github.com/repos/lidge-jun/opencodex/releases/latest')
		.then((res) => (res.ok ? res.json() : Promise.reject(res.status)))
		.then((release: { tag_name?: string; assets?: { name?: string; browser_download_url?: string }[] }) => {
			const patterns: Record<string, RegExp> = {
				dmg: /-macos\.dmg$/,
				msi: /-windows-x64\.msi$/,
				appimage: /-linux-x86_64\.AppImage$/,
				deb: /-linux-amd64\.deb$/,
			};
			for (const asset of release.assets ?? []) {
				const key = Object.keys(patterns).find((k) => asset.name && patterns[k].test(asset.name));
				if (!key || !asset.browser_download_url) continue;
				const link = document.querySelector<HTMLAnchorElement>(`[data-lp-asset="${key}"]`);
				if (link) link.href = asset.browser_download_url;
			}
			const version = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-lp-version]');
			if (version && release.tag_name) {
				version.textContent = release.tag_name;
				version.closest('[data-lp-version-wrap]')?.removeAttribute('hidden');
			}
		})
		.catch(() => {});
</script>
